com&gt; Tested-by: John Carey &lt;ranix@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: John Carey &lt;ranix@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="328470" owner_email="ranix@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/70/328470/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3b64fe898beea5222c64074b3ffee2e86f10eecf" commit="43a96bb5d5959fdf040c2cde7b5fd3de2a78ef42" commit_message="test_droid: make serial # optional  Users need not specify the serial # by default when they only have one device attached.  This also fixes the serial number parser to allow dashes as this shows up in the emulator:  emulator-5554 device  BUG=b:27301538 TEST=read the doc TEST=`./test_droid.py brillo_Gtests` works w/emu (auto-detected) TEST=`./test_droid.py brillo_Gtests -s emulator-5554` works w/emu TEST=`./test_droid.py brillo_Gtests -s alsdkjf` fails as it can't find device  Change-Id: I3b64fe898beea5222c64074b3ffee2e86f10eecf Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329140 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329140" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/40/329140/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I741bcd29452250c81d3aa6fd63e617ff657774d5" commit="ce9b8468288b6903be8e166bcd97849008da327d" commit_message="BACKPORT: ASoC: rt5514: add rt5514 codec driver  This is the initial codec driver for rt5514. The codec includes a low power DSP for voice wake up. The register address is incremental by 4 in the DSP memory map. In order to recover the codec settings in the codec mode and manipulate the DSP mode for voice wake up, we use the multi-level register map. One is for ALSA API in codec mode that can be recovered by cache before recording. Another is for DSP related settings that can be accessed with 32bit address of the DSP in the application of voice wake up.  Signed-off-by: Oder Chiou &lt;oder_chiou@realtek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 4a6180ea7399b945cd380dc63e2e8118f9b432d3)  [pc.liao: req_sequence is not defined in Chrome OS 3.18, so use reg_default instead]  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50078 TEST=oak-rev6, sound capture works  Change-Id: I741bcd29452250c81d3aa6fd63e617ff657774d5 Signed-off-by: Koro Chen &lt;koro.chen@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321582 Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321582" owner_email="koro.chen@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/82/321582/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idf33ffb190d919f6015a3c676d6b80e7ebe69a46" commit="157f49cf784517764f60cb6f560c942064eb80e0" commit_message="crash: Disable flaky test  BUG=b:27366531 TEST=cros_workon_make chromeos-base/crash-reporter --test  Change-Id: Idf33ffb190d919f6015a3c676d6b80e7ebe69a46 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329401 Commit-Ready: Dominik Laskowski &lt;domlaskowski@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dominik Laskowski &lt;domlaskowski@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329401" owner_email="domlaskowski@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/01/329401/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I77e8650fd9f6ecea933fa49138fc37a2eee5d636" commit="9637561901e4d5bfa68700f75fae4d964d610e42" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm: rockchip: Add the shared fence before calling the callback  In vop_win_update_sync() we need to move drm_reservation_cb_done() after reservation_object_add_shared_fence() because:  * When we call drm_reservation_cb_done(), it's possible (iff PREEMPT)   that vop_win_update_cb() will be called right away (if all the fences   attached to the reservation have already been signaled).  * If vop_win_update_cb() runs it will call vop_win_update_commit()  * When vop_win_update_commit() runs, then if (!needs_vblank) then we   call vop_win_update()  * vop_win_update() will set vop_win-&gt;pending_fence = NULL  ...then we end up using vop_win-&gt;pending_fence right away and pass it to reservation_object_add_shared_fence().  If it's been NULLed that's not so valid.  BUG=chromium:586711 TEST=See steps in bug  Change-Id: I77e8650fd9f6ecea933fa49138fc37a2eee5d636 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329159 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329159" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/59/329159/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7967.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>